{"title":"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/5/a55ebc55eb68924a644773605753defcf65d8071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAC}= \\angle{BDC}= 36^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"15\" /> , <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0884d3de022586a931e71a7e1c97d25e9fbd3c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBD}= 18^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"105\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f95fb05be898ec9d7c67983964703cef63ef7a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BAC}= 72^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />. The diagonals and intersect at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> . Determine the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982639815a9c7d84ed18958a7a169f823b05fcab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{APD}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let I be the intersection between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1c5b18c49288ec49cdffc2fb97a43d7e089243b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(DP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" /> and the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c3b923ba663115bc49fdc8471e956b38880b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> \nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0ba3b6b3e7e3b8346bcc67c18aacec3199e5a84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAI}=\\angle{PAI}=36/2°=18°$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c5f4c7ec03d05a0a2d928158775cde56e071c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAI}=18°=\\angle{CBD}=\\angle{CBI}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"252\" height=\"14\" />\nWe can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e4dc32c4910d00feaa0c3421775a8e1452a247d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> are on a same circle.\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e9c3a64f34fc2e9767330eece36d0c3ee73efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ICB}=180-\\angle{IAB}=180-\\angle{IAC}-\\angle{CAB}=180-18-72=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"554\" height=\"16\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b70fdafbcda274395b763223d6887942c8204482.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBD}=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1ebeed6e209c996a16c1cbe3fb4cc22890fe8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CDB}=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87eb16f92d42e60c576fb214350a0f47aac27be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126=\\angle{DCB}=\\angle{ICB}+\\angle{ICD}=90+\\angle{ICD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"377\" height=\"16\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bc5b99b93e79f350f463f0b3aa15b32aef00a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ICD}=36=\\angle{BDC}=\\angle{IDC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"254\" height=\"14\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is on the angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c3b923ba663115bc49fdc8471e956b38880b11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> and on the mediator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />.\nThe first posibility is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the south pole of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is on the circle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6250647b3666c03d1363b3a401f37c1d9db3c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> but we can easily seen that's not possible\nThe second possibility is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6250647b3666c03d1363b3a401f37c1d9db3c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. So because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466e43f4c503703554dfd6b06aed4a84598d3b8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAC}=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6250647b3666c03d1363b3a401f37c1d9db3c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22d3391c298e332fdd1a6cd93743d98e54065b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADC}=72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"14\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/9/b9941569d1a8f19100eae94dbbfc5d6b18925b74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{APD}=180-\\angle{PAD}-\\angle{PDA}=180-36-(\\angle{ADC}-\\angle{PDC})=180-36-72+36=108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"754\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO\" title=\"2007 JBMO\">2007 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213831\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 187/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 868/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 36/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5494/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.707      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    7.707      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:26688:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213831 and revision id 217680. Rendering wa